# Design Intent

The Hero should immediately communicate:

- Premium private touring
- Authentic South African experiences
- Personal service
- Luxury without excess
- Wine country
- Scenic beauty

The interface should feel calm, spacious and inviting.

Visitors should feel inspired rather than sold to.

---

# Layout

The Hero consists of two distinct layers.

## Layer 1

Full-width visual background.

The background image shall span the full viewport width.

## Layer 2

Shared content container.

The Hero content shall be constrained within the standard Design System container.

Example

-------------------------------------------------------

Full-width Hero Background

+-----------------------------------------------------+

        +-----------------------------------+

        Hero Content

        Heading

        Paragraph

        CTA Buttons

        +-----------------------------------+

+-----------------------------------------------------+

This alignment shall match all subsequent landing page sections.

---

# Hero Image

Requirements

- Authentic photography
- High resolution
- Landscape orientation
- Natural lighting
- Cinematic composition
- Optimised for responsive delivery

Preferred subjects

- Cape Winelands
- Stellenbosch vineyards
- Mountain passes
- Boutique wineries
- Luxury touring
- Scenic roads
- Table Mountain in the distance

Avoid

- Generic stock photography
- Crowded tourist scenes
- Over-saturated editing
- Artificial HDR effects

The image shall support future replacement through a CMS.

---

# Hero Overlay

A subtle overlay may be used to improve text readability.

The overlay shall not obscure the photography.

Overlay styling shall remain component-specific and shall not become a Design Token.

