---

# Accessibility

Requirements

- Semantic HTML
- Single H1 element
- Descriptive alt text (if using an <img>)
- Decorative imagery marked appropriately where applicable
- Keyboard-accessible buttons
- WCAG AA colour contrast
- Visible focus indicators

---

# Performance

Requirements

- Responsive image delivery
- Lazy loading where appropriate (do not lazy-load the Largest Contentful Paint image)
- Modern image formats (WebP preferred)
- Minimal JavaScript
- Zero layout shift (CLS)

Target

Lighthouse Performance ≥95

---

# Animation

Animations shall be subtle.

Examples

- Fade-in headline
- Gentle button appearance
- Slight image fade
- Scroll indicator fade

Maximum duration

```
300ms
```

Animations shall consume DS-001 transition tokens where applicable.

---

# JavaScript Responsibilities

hero.js shall only manage behaviour.

Examples

- Optional scroll indicator behaviour
- Reduced-motion support
- Future enhancement hooks

No presentation logic shall reside in JavaScript.

---

# CSS Responsibilities

hero.css shall define:

- Layout
- Hero spacing
- Responsive typography
- Overlay styling
- Button positioning
- Responsive behaviour
- Animation classes

All reusable values shall consume DS-001 Design Tokens.

---

# Acceptance Criteria

Implementation is complete when:

- Hero renders correctly on desktop.
- Hero renders correctly on tablet.
- Hero renders correctly on mobile.
- Typography follows DS-001.
- Colours consume Design Tokens.
- Buttons consume shared button styles.
- Responsive behaviour is verified.
- Accessibility requirements are satisfied.
- Performance targets are met.
- No inline CSS or JavaScript is present.

